# .dockerignore for a site built with the kit's Dockerfile.azure (copy it to the
# site root as .dockerignore). It keeps the build context small and keeps host
# build output, test artefacts and local secrets out of the image. The Dockerfile
# copies only package*.json, tsconfig*.json, site.json, src/, vendor/affiliate-kit/
# and DOCKER_EXTRA_PATHS, so nothing listed here is needed by the build.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
.git
.github
tests
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
agents
prompts
scripts/local
vendor/affiliate-kit/unit
vendor/affiliate-kit/tests
vendor/affiliate-kit/fixtures
*.log
.env
.env.*
deploy.env
secrets.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.pfx
